{
  "title": "Recipe sync cursor can skip concurrent commits",
  "description": "`GET /api/recipes/sync` captures `sync_timestamp` before its \
SELECT, returns it as the next cursor, and later filters changes with \
timestamps strictly greater than that cursor. A concurrent recipe or tag \
transaction can receive a `created_at`, `updated_at`, or `deleted_at` at or \
before the cursor, then commit after the sync SELECT has taken its snapshot. \
The row is invisible to that sync and excluded from every later delta, so an \
iOS cache can remain stale until a forced full sync.\n\
\n\
Choose and implement a race-safe change cursor or reconciliation strategy \
before expanding recipe sync for full local search. Add a deterministic API \
regression test that coordinates an uncommitted create/update, tag change, or \
soft delete across the sync snapshot and proves the next sync returns it. The \
fix must preserve idempotent application of repeated changes and soft-delete \
tombstones.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
  "type": "bug",
  "labels": [
    "api",
